{"id":"scripts/omnibar-acceptance.mjs","pkg":"scripts","kind":"script","lines":272,"commentLines":53,"header":["I run every question in eval/router-acceptance.json through the REAL front door, GET /api/ai-search, exactly as the omnibar's Enter key does (HANDOFF_dsp-intranet_front-path.md: \"test only through the front door\"), and I record for each one: the route that answered, the latency, and pass/fail against the expected facts. It changes no app code, writes nothing to the database, and never calls the feedback endpoints.","----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------","BEFORE YOU RUN IT: local dev and Vercel use the SAME online resources (Supabase, Groq, Gemini).","* Every question that is not a holiday question makes at least one Groq call, and each call carries the whole schema prompt (several thousand tokens). The free tier allows 200,000 tokens a day, so a full run does NOT fit in one day. Therefore I added these controls: --no-model run only the questions the deterministic holiday parser should answer (no tokens) --max-model-calls N stop cleanly after N model calls (the server reports the exact number) --max-tokens N stop cleanly once the questions so far have used N tokens: the right control for the 200,000-a-day free allowance (e.g. --max-tokens 150000 leaves room for the app itself) --resume FILE continue an earlier results file: questions already answered are kept, the rest run --model-pause MS wait this long after a question that used the model (default 40000). Measured on the first real run: one model call is about 4,900 tokens and the free tier allows about 8,000 tokens a minute, so calls closer together than ~40 s just sit in the app's 429 wait. Use 0 to let the app wait by itself. The server console prints the real token count of every call (\"Every call prints one line with the tokens\").","* Executive Deep Synthesis questions send up to ten circulars to the model (the most expensive), so I run them only with --eds AND --cookie. Since step 25a the server takes WHO is calling from the login session, never from the browser's ticket parameter, so the harness needs a real executive session: log in to the app in your browser, open the developer tools > Application > Cookies, and pass the value like this: --cookie \"next-auth.session-token=PASTE-THE-VALUE\" (it is sent only with the synthesis questions, never written to the results). The two SEC- security probes need no cookie: they check that synthesis is REFUSED without a login.","USAGE (from the project root, with `npm run dev` running in another terminal): node scripts/omnibar-acceptance.mjs --list what is in the set node scripts/omnibar-acceptance.mjs --no-model --tag local-free the free part first (holidays, Bad Queries) node scripts/omnibar-acceptance.mjs --regression --tag local only the records verified on screen before node scripts/omnibar-acceptance.mjs --source A,HC --tag local by source (A,B,K,H,F,HC,S,CB,G) node scripts/omnibar-acceptance.mjs --base https://YOUR-APP.vercel.app --tag vercel node scripts/omnibar-acceptance.mjs --compare eval/results/a.json eval/results/b.json Other options: --only ID,ID --area NAME --eds --with FLAG --pause MS (default 1500) --yes --dry-run --raw (save every sanitised answer, not only failures) --exec-ticket 4xxxxx --out DIR OUTPUT: eval/results/acceptance-<tag>-<timestamp>.json (all data) and .md (the report to read or send back). Personal data: I remove people's P.No. and masked contacts from everything written to disk (see the report)."],"symbols":[{"name":"argv","kind":"constant","exported":false,"line":51,"sig":"const argv = process.argv.slice(2)","type":"","doc":["------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ arguments"],"members":[],"items":0,"id":"583a91be6f-argv","usedBy":[]},{"name":"has","kind":"function","exported":false,"line":52,"async":false,"sig":"const has = (n) =>","params":[{"name":